## Known Bugs Fixed (DO NOT REINTRODUCE)

| Bug | Fix |
|-----|-----|
| `replaceTikTokBlockquote(markdown, url)` called without url | Function extracts URL internally from block |
| Category scraper used Firecrawl v1 | Now v2 |
| `$.html()` returns full document | Use `$('body').html() \|\| $.html()` |
| `[[EMBED:YOUTUBE:abc123]]` example in system prompt | Removed — causes hallucination |
| `stale-while-revalidate=86400` | Changed to 120s |
| `.catch()` on Supabase insert | Use try/catch instead |
| `extractAllEmbedsFromMarkdown` return type not used | `markdownContent = extractAllEmbedsFromMarkdown(markdownContent)` |
| og:title containing full article body | Guard: title.length > 100 → H1 fallback |
| LLM expands title with article content | shortText=true uses dedicated headline prompt |
| TL;DR duplication | createArticleEnhancementPrompt() uses `---\n${content}` not "return full article" |
| Short Turkish words in validation | Removed: için, göre, kadar, ile, ve, de, da, ki |
| Title has `**markdown**` bold | Strip `***` in translator.js translateArticle() after translation |
| Truncated URLs bypass duplicate check | 3-layer: exact URL + slug prefix + content_hash |
| `__WIDGET_N__` leaks into description | Strip placeholders after description translation in translateArticle() |
| wp-content in regex fallback | Filter /wp-content/, /wp-includes/, /wp-json/ in _regexFallback() |
| Same article, different URL = duplicate | content_hash (SHA256 of normalized original_title) stored in DB |

## Duplicate Detection (3 Layers)

```
Layer 1: source_url exact match (fastest)
Layer 2: slug prefix match (handles truncated URLs)
Layer 3: content_hash match (handles same article, different URL)
```

- `content_hash` = SHA256(normalize(original_turkish_title))
- Stored in `tech_news_articles.content_hash` column
- `isContentHashDuplicate(title)` called after scraping, before translation
- This saves Ollama/Groq API credits — no translation wasted on duplicates
- In-memory URL dedupe happens before DB duplicate filtering and before `MAX_ARTICLES_PER_RUN`
- `MAX_ARTICLES_PER_RUN` must cap prioritized *new* articles, not raw discovered links

